# THE WORK EDITOR, which is the generic editor pointed at work.
#
# The format is Obsidian's and the engine renders it. Nothing here is a second
# grammar, and nothing in the renderer knows what a token is.
#
# A DECLARED GROUP IS ALWAYS DRAWN, with nothing in it if nothing matches. What
# it names goes on existing whether or not a token is in that state today, and a
# heading that comes and goes is a heading nobody can aim at. A group nobody
# declared comes from the data, and one of those is gone the moment it empties.
#
# A DECLARED GROUP IS A QUERY AND NOT A PLACE. A row draws under every group
# whose filter takes it, and under its bucket as well. So a state needs a group
# NAMED FOR IT or the page never says which state the row is in: here says yes
# to four states at once, and a token whose only group was here was one the
# owner could not tell from three other kinds of work.
#
# A PIN IS AN ORDERING AND NOT AN EXISTENCE. It names a declared group and puts
# it on top, so unpinning leaves the group where the grouping puts it.
#
# A GROUP THE DATA MADE IS PINNED WITH ITS FILTER WRITTEN IN, and this file goes
# on declaring nothing about it. So unpinning takes the whole entry away, and a
# bucket somebody invented goes back to disappearing when it empties.
#
# EVERY STATE A WORKER IS HANDED OR HOLDS HAS A GROUP OF ITS OWN, and
# src/engine/workview_test.go is what holds that: it asks the engine for those
# states, renders this file, and requires each one to draw under a group of its
# own name. imp_open and imp_in_work were missing, so the owner read a token in
# work as work in no state at all.
#
# HERE IS EVERYTHING AT THE CURRENT STATE, and there are no states above the
# token yet, so here is everything that is open or in work. It carries in_work
# as well as open so a person sees what is being done and not only what waits.
#
# THE GROUPING GROUPS BY THE BUCKET AND BY NOTHING ELSE. It read
# if(bucket, bucket, status), so a token with no bucket grouped under its state
# and drew a second group beside the query named after that state. The fallback
# was invisible while a declared group took its rows first, and every state drew
# twice the moment a query stopped taking them. A bucket is where a person put a
# row. A state is the engine's word for where the row is, and there is a query
# for each one already.

# A COLUMN IS NAMED WHAT THE NOTE NAMES IT. displayName exists for a heading
# the owner wants to read differently, and renaming status to state or assignee
# to who is not that: it hides where the value came from and nobody can filter
# on a word that is not in the file.
properties:
  title:
    opensNote: true

filters:
  and:
    - type == "work"
    - status != "imp_done"
    - status != "aborted"

groups:
  # YOURS IS EVERYTHING OF YOURS THAT NEEDS WORK FROM YOU. It mirrored
  # here, so a token assigned to the person while it still carried a draft sat
  # under spec_open and the group meant to hold their work was empty. A status
  # is moved by a pull and never by a keystroke, rightly, so there was no way to
  # put a token in front of the person it belongs to. The view is what was
  # wrong. What is left out is what somebody else holds, which is the four
  # waiting states, and the backlog, which is nobody's work yet. It is written
  # as what is excluded rather than as what is included, so a state nobody
  # anticipated shows up here rather than disappearing.
  - name: yours
    filter: assignee == "human" && status != "backlogged" && status != "spec_submitted" && status != "spec_in_review" && status != "imp_submitted" && status != "imp_in_review"
  # HERE IS FOUR STATES AND IT USED TO BE TWO. The engine's states are two
  # halves with the same four verbs, so somebody who has learned one half has
  # learned the other, and this filter named the second half only. Fourteen
  # drafts sat below the rule with nothing on the page saying they were work in
  # flight. It was written when one agent drafted at a time and nothing noticed.
  #
  # THE FOUR ARE HandedOut(worker) AND HeldBy(worker), which is where
  # src/engine/arrival.go declares which states a worker is handed and which it
  # holds. A .base file cannot ask the engine for a set, so the names are typed
  # here and src/engine/here_test.go is what holds them: it reads those two
  # functions and requires this filter to answer yes to every state they name
  # and no to every state somebody else holds. A twelfth state joining either
  # one goes red there rather than going quiet here.
  - name: here
    filter: status == "imp_open" || status == "imp_in_work" || status == "spec_open" || status == "spec_in_work"
  - name: backlogged
    filter: status == "backlogged"
  - name: spec_open
    filter: status == "spec_open"
  - name: spec_in_work
    filter: status == "spec_in_work"
  - name: spec_submitted
    filter: status == "spec_submitted"
  - name: spec_in_review
    filter: status == "spec_in_review"
  - name: imp_open
    filter: status == "imp_open"
  - name: imp_in_work
    filter: status == "imp_in_work"
  - name: imp_submitted
    filter: status == "imp_submitted"
  - name: imp_in_review
    filter: status == "imp_in_review"
pinned:
  - yours
  - here

views:
  - type: table
    name: left
    counts:
      - name: in work
        filter: status == "imp_in_work" || status == "spec_in_work"
        outOf: status == "imp_in_work" || status == "spec_in_work" || status == "imp_open" || status == "spec_open"
      - name: in review
        filter: status == "imp_in_review" || status == "spec_in_review"
        outOf: status == "imp_in_review" || status == "spec_in_review" || status == "imp_submitted" || status == "spec_submitted"
    order:
      - title
      - status
      - assignee
    columnSize:
      title: 300
      status: 110
      assignee: 71
      blocked: 543
    groupBy:
      - property: bucket
        sets: bucket
        direction: ASC
    collapsed:
      - backlogged
    sort:
      - property: assignee
        direction: DESC
  - type: table
    name: right
    counts:
      - name: in work
        filter: status == "imp_in_work" || status == "spec_in_work"
        outOf: status == "imp_in_work" || status == "spec_in_work" || status == "imp_open" || status == "spec_open"
      - name: in review
        filter: status == "imp_in_review" || status == "spec_in_review"
        outOf: status == "imp_in_review" || status == "spec_in_review" || status == "imp_submitted" || status == "spec_submitted"
    order:
      - title
      - status
    groupBy:
      - property: bucket
        sets: bucket
        direction: ASC
    collapsed:
      - backlogged
